IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oas-core-periods`
IMPORT `oas-core-pension`
IMPORT `oa2-indexation`
IMPORT `oa2-part2-eligibility`
IMPORT `oa2-part2-amount`
IMPORT `oa2-part2-income`
IMPORT `oa2-part2-spouse`
IMPORT `oa2-part2-payment`
IMPORT `oa2-part3-amount`
IMPORT `oa2-part3-spouse-allowance`
IMPORT `oa2-part3-survivor-allowance`
IMPORT `oa2-part3-payment`

-- Old Age Security Act, R.S.C. 1985, c. O-9, Parts II and III (ss 10 to 26) -- THE SEAT LAYER (piece oa2).
--
-- SEAT: a person who is 65 or older, or approaching it, asking whether they qualify for the Guaranteed Income Supplement
-- or an Allowance, how much they would receive, and what they must do or tell the Minister.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the oa2 modules imported above as the questions that person would
-- ask. Nothing here is new law: every question calls a rule of a layer-1 module and restates none of them. Each question
-- has @export and @desc, takes plain inputs (yes/no, numbers, dates, a choice from the modules' own lists), and the
-- records the modules expect (the facts about a pensioner and a month, the facts about a person who may be paid an
-- Allowance, the special qualification facts, a sentence of imprisonment, the figures for an estimate) are built inside
-- each question, in its WHERE, from those answers.
--
-- Rights and duties come in pairs (Hohfeld). The other party's side of each relation is a plain input here: whether the
-- Minister has approved, waived, deemed or been satisfied is a fact the person can state. The pairs are listed in
-- NOTES.md under "Jural relations".
--
-- Where an input is optional (the date something happened, if it did) it is a MAYBE type and the @desc says "leave blank
-- if none". Where a rule of the module needs a record field the person cannot state, the question says so below:
--   * "Placeholder": a record field the rule called never reads is given a fixed value, with a comment on the question.
--   * "Fixed value": a field the rule does read is fixed because the seat knows it (here: the month in which the person
--     dies is left blank, because the person is asking about their own entitlement while living).
-- Figures the government publishes (the maximum supplement for a quarter, the supplement equivalent, the figure for A,
-- the Consumer Price Index) are inputs: the person copies them from the published tables.
-- Dates the text does not give (the month paragraph 19(6)(e) and subsection 21(7.1) came into force) are inputs too.
-- Prescribed figures from the Regulations (piece oa3) enter as inputs: the earlier date of s 23(1), the months of s 18.2(1).
--
-- The Regulations and the sections of Parts I and IV of the Act are not encoded here; see "Cross-references out of my
-- ranges" in NOTES.md.

§ `Old Age Security Act -- Part II: the questions of a person 65 or older, or approaching it`

§§ `Whether the Guaranteed Income Supplement can be paid to me (ss 10, 11)`

-- ss 10, 11. A "pensioner" is a person whose application for the pension has been approved. A supplement may be paid for a
-- month if you applied (or the Minister waived or deemed your application) and payment has been approved, no pension bar
-- applies, you have not been out of Canada for six months, you are not barred by a sponsor's undertaking, and so on. The
-- Minister's side of each relation (approving, waiving, deeming) is taken as a fact you can state.
@export May I be paid the Guaranteed Income Supplement for this month (ss 10, 11)?
GIVEN `the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? (give any date in that month)
      `my pension application has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your application for the Old Age Security pension been approved?
      `I have applied for the supplement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for the Guaranteed Income Supplement?
      `payment of my supplement has been approved for the months in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has payment of the supplement been approved for the months in the year you are asking about?
      `the Minister has treated me as having applied and been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister treated you as having applied for the supplement and been approved, because your allowance stopped when you turned 65?
      `the Minister waived my application when I turned 65` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister waive the need for you to apply for the supplement when you turned 65?
      `the Minister waived my application for the payment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister waive the need for you to apply for this payment period, because you had applied for an earlier one?
      `the month my application was received, treated as made, or waived` IS A DATE @desc In which month was your application received, treated as made, or waived? (give any date in that month)
      `no pension may be paid to me for the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is no pension payable to you for the month you are asking about?
      `I am out of Canada for the whole month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you out of Canada for the whole of the month you are asking about?
      `the month I left Canada` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc In which month did you leave Canada? (leave blank if you have not left)
      `I have stayed outside Canada since I left` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you stayed outside Canada ever since you left?
      `I am not resident in Canada throughout the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not resident in Canada throughout the month you are asking about?
      `the day I stopped residing in Canada` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day did you stop residing in Canada? (leave blank if you have not stopped)
      `a sponsor's undertaking is in effect for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a sponsor's undertaking under the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act in effect in respect of you during the month?
      `I was qualified for a pension or an allowance just before paragraph 11(8)(a) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you qualified to receive a pension or an allowance immediately before the day on which paragraph 11(8)(a) of the Act came into force?
      `an event described in the regulations has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an event happened that the Old Age Security Regulations say lifts the limit on sponsored persons?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be paid the Guaranteed Income Supplement for this month` IF
    `s 11: a supplement may be paid to the pensioner for the month` `the month I am asking about` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 11: Facts about a pensioner and a month` WITH
            `the person's application for a pension has been approved` IS `my pension application has been approved`
            `an application for payment of a supplement has been made by the pensioner` IS `I have applied for the supplement`
            `payment of the supplement for months in that year has been approved under this Part` IS `payment of my supplement has been approved for the months in the year`
            `the Minister has deemed an application to have been made and approved under subsection 11(3)` IS `the Minister has treated me as having applied and been approved`
            `the Minister has waived the requirement for an application under subsection 11(3.1)` IS `the Minister waived my application when I turned 65`
            `the Minister has waived the requirement for an application under subsection 11(4)` IS `the Minister waived my application for the payment period`
            `the month in which the application is received or is deemed to have been made or in which the requirement for an application has been waived` IS `the month my application was received, treated as made, or waived`
            `no pension may be paid to the pensioner for the month` IS `no pension may be paid to me for the month`
            `the pensioner is absent from Canada throughout the month` IS `I am out of Canada for the whole month`
            `the month in which the pensioner left Canada` IS `the month I left Canada`
            `the pensioner has remained outside Canada since leaving` IS `I have stayed outside Canada since I left`
            `the pensioner is not resident in Canada throughout the month` IS `I am not resident in Canada throughout the month`
            `the day on which the pensioner ceased to reside in Canada` IS `the day I stopped residing in Canada`
            `an undertaking by a sponsor is in effect in respect of the pensioner during the month` IS `a sponsor's undertaking is in effect for me`
            `the pensioner was qualified to receive a pension or an allowance immediately before the day on which paragraph 11(8)(a) comes into force` IS `I was qualified for a pension or an allowance just before paragraph 11(8)(a) came into force`
            `an event as provided by the regulations has occurred` IS `an event described in the regulations has occurred`


-- s 11(7)(a). No supplement may be paid for a month more than eleven months before the month your application is received.
-- Placeholder: the rule called reads only the month of the application; every other field is given a fixed value.
@export In which month is the earliest for which a supplement can be paid to me, if I apply late (s 11(7)(a))?
GIVEN `the month my application was received, treated as made, or waived` IS A DATE @desc In which month was your application received, treated as made, or waived? (give any date in that month)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `In which month is the earliest for which a supplement can be paid to me` IS
    `s 11(7)(a): the earliest month for which a supplement may be paid` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 11: Facts about a pensioner and a month` WITH
            `the person's application for a pension has been approved` IS FALSE
            `an application for payment of a supplement has been made by the pensioner` IS FALSE
            `payment of the supplement for months in that year has been approved under this Part` IS FALSE
            `the Minister has deemed an application to have been made and approved under subsection 11(3)` IS FALSE
            `the Minister has waived the requirement for an application under subsection 11(3.1)` IS FALSE
            `the Minister has waived the requirement for an application under subsection 11(4)` IS FALSE
            `the month in which the application is received or is deemed to have been made or in which the requirement for an application has been waived` IS `the month my application was received, treated as made, or waived`
            `no pension may be paid to the pensioner for the month` IS FALSE
            `the pensioner is absent from Canada throughout the month` IS FALSE
            `the month in which the pensioner left Canada` IS NOTHING
            `the pensioner has remained outside Canada since leaving` IS FALSE
            `the pensioner is not resident in Canada throughout the month` IS FALSE
            `the day on which the pensioner ceased to reside in Canada` IS NOTHING
            `an undertaking by a sponsor is in effect in respect of the pensioner during the month` IS FALSE
            `the pensioner was qualified to receive a pension or an allowance immediately before the day on which paragraph 11(8)(a) comes into force` IS FALSE
            `an event as provided by the regulations has occurred` IS FALSE


-- s 11(3.2), (3.3). Before waiving your application when you turn 65 the Minister must tell you in writing what information the
-- Minister holds. If it is wrong you must file a statement correcting it, by the day before you turn 65 (this is your duty;
-- the Minister's duty to tell you is the correlative right).
@export By what day must I file a statement correcting inaccuracies if the Minister tells me my application for the supplement will be waived (s 11(3.3))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I file a statement correcting inaccuracies` IS
    `s 11(3.3): the last day on which the person may file the statement correcting inaccuracies` `my date of birth`


-- s 11(3.4). You may decline the waiver by telling the Minister in writing by the day before you turn 65 (your power; the Minister
-- is then liable to deal with your application in the ordinary way).
@export Did I decline the waiver in time (s 11(3.4))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day I told the Minister in writing that I decline` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you tell the Minister in writing that you decline the waiver?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I decline the waiver in time` IF
    `s 11(3.4): the person has declined the waiver in time` `my date of birth` `the day I told the Minister in writing that I decline`


-- s 11(5). If the Minister waived your application for a payment period, the Minister may later notify you in writing that you must
-- apply for later months, but not later than fifteen days before the first of those months.
@export By what day may the Minister notify me that I must apply for later months (s 11(5))?
GIVEN `the first of the months for which I must apply` IS A DATE @desc What is the first month for which you must apply? (give any date in that month)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day may the Minister notify me that I must apply for later months` IS
    `s 11(5): the last day on which the Minister may give the notice` `the first of the months for which I must apply`


§§ `How much supplement (ss 12, 12.1)`

-- s 12(2), (3), (4). From the quarter that begins July 1, 2005 the maximum is the previous maximum times the ratio of the price
-- indexes, never less than before, plus the fixed increases of 2006 and 2007. A quarter that begins on or before June 30, 2005 is not
-- covered by this rule: the answer is blank (NOTHING).
@export What is the maximum monthly supplement for a payment quarter after June 2005 (s 12(2))?
GIVEN `the first day of the quarter` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the payment quarter begin?
      `my situation for the quarter` IS A `s 12(1): Situation of the pensioner` @desc Which describes you on the day before the quarter began: a person with no spouse or common-law partner to whom a pension may be paid in the quarter; a person whose spouse or partner has no pension payable yet in the quarter; or a person whose spouse or partner has a pension payable from this month?
      `the maximum supplement for the previous quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the maximum supplement that could be paid for any month in the three months before this quarter, in dollars?
      `the price index for the first adjustment quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to this payment quarter?
      `the price index for the second adjustment quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to this payment quarter?
      `the earlier index still deemed to apply` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc If an earlier fall in the price index has not yet been made up, what is the index of the earlier second adjustment quarter still deemed to apply? (leave blank if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the maximum monthly supplement for a payment quarter` IS
    CONSIDER (`s 12(2): the maximum supplement for a payment quarter commencing after June 30, 2005` `the first day of the quarter` `my situation for the quarter` `the maximum supplement for the previous quarter` `the price index for the first adjustment quarter` `the price index for the second adjustment quarter` `the earlier index still deemed to apply`)
    WHEN JUST outcome THEN JUST (outcome's `the amount for the payment quarter`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING


-- s 12(5). Your supplement for a month is [(A - B) x C] - D/2 where A is the maximum supplement plus your full pension, B is your
-- monthly pension, C is your special qualifying factor (one unless you have lived in Canada under ten years) and D is your monthly
-- base income rounded down to a multiple of two dollars. A result below zero is paid as zero (fork F-12-2 in NOTES.md).
@export How much supplement can I be paid for this month (s 12(5))?
GIVEN `the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? (give any date in that month)
      `the maximum supplement that could be paid to me for the month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum monthly supplement for your situation for this month, in dollars?
      `my full monthly pension before any increase for deferring` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of your full monthly pension for the month, before any increase for deferring it, in dollars?
      `my full monthly pension after any increase for deferring` IS A NUMBER @desc What is that amount after any increase for deferring your pension, in dollars?
      `my monthly pension before any increase for deferring` IS A NUMBER @desc What monthly pension is payable to you before any increase for deferring it, in dollars?
      `my monthly pension after any increase for deferring` IS A NUMBER @desc What monthly pension is payable to you after any increase for deferring it, in dollars?
      `my years of residence in Canada after age 18` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years have you lived in Canada since you turned 18, counted to the last day of the previous month?
      `a pension or allowance was payable to me for March 1996 or an earlier month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a pension or an allowance payable to you for the month of March 1996 or an earlier month?
      `a pension or allowance was payable to me for January 2001 or an earlier month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a pension or an allowance payable to you for the month of January 2001 or an earlier month?
      `before March 7, 1996 I was living in Canada as a citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before March 7, 1996, were you living in Canada as a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident?
      `my monthly base income` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your monthly base income, in dollars? (one-twelfth of your income for the base calendar year, as the Act adjusts it)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much supplement can I be paid for this month` IS
    `s 12(5): the amount of the supplement that may be paid for the month` `the month I am asking about` `the maximum supplement that could be paid to me for the month` `my full monthly pension before any increase for deferring` `my full monthly pension after any increase for deferring` `my monthly pension before any increase for deferring` `my monthly pension after any increase for deferring` `my special qualification facts` `my monthly base income`
    WHERE
        `my special qualification facts` MEANS `Special qualification facts` WITH
            `years of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age, as of the last day of the immediately preceding month` IS `my years of residence in Canada after age 18`
            `a pension or allowance was payable to the person for the month of March 1996 or an earlier month` IS `a pension or allowance was payable to me for March 1996 or an earlier month`
            `a pension or allowance was payable to the person for the month of January 2001 or an earlier month` IS `a pension or allowance was payable to me for January 2001 or an earlier month`
            `before March 7, 1996 the person was residing in Canada as a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident` IS `before March 7, 1996 I was living in Canada as a citizen or permanent resident`


-- s 12(6). Monthly base income is one-twelfth of your income for the base calendar year, or a combination with your spouse's or
-- partner's income depending on whether a pension is payable to your spouse or partner, as the paragraph for your situation says.
@export What is my monthly base income for the supplement (s 12(6))?
GIVEN `the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? (give any date in that month)
      `on the day before the current payment period I was the spouse or common-law partner of a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On the day before the current payment period began, were you the spouse or common-law partner of a person?
      `a pension may be paid to that person for a month in the current payment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May a pension be paid to that person for any month in the current payment period?
      `the first month for which a pension may be paid to my spouse or partner` IS A DATE @desc What is the first month for which a pension may be paid to your spouse or common-law partner? (give any date if there is none)
      `my income for the base calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your income for the base calendar year, in dollars?
      `my spouse's or partner's income for the base calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your spouse's or common-law partner's income for the base calendar year, in dollars?
      `my full monthly pension without regard to section 7(5)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the full monthly pension calculated without regard to subsection 7(5), in dollars?
      `my years of residence in Canada after age 18` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years have you lived in Canada since you turned 18, counted to the last day of the previous month?
      `a pension or allowance was payable to me for March 1996 or an earlier month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a pension or an allowance payable to you for the month of March 1996 or an earlier month?
      `a pension or allowance was payable to me for January 2001 or an earlier month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a pension or an allowance payable to you for the month of January 2001 or an earlier month?
      `before March 7, 1996 I was living in Canada as a citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before March 7, 1996, were you living in Canada as a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my monthly base income for the supplement` IS
    `s 12(6): the monthly base income for the month` `my situation` `the month I am asking about` `the first month for which a pension may be paid to my spouse or partner` `my income for the base calendar year` `my spouse's or partner's income for the base calendar year` `my full monthly pension without regard to section 7(5)` `my special qualification facts`
    WHERE
        `my situation` MEANS `s 12(6): the situation of the applicant` `on the day before the current payment period I was the spouse or common-law partner of a person` `a pension may be paid to that person for a month in the current payment period`
        `my special qualification facts` MEANS `Special qualification facts` WITH
            `years of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age, as of the last day of the immediately preceding month` IS `my years of residence in Canada after age 18`
            `a pension or allowance was payable to the person for the month of March 1996 or an earlier month` IS `a pension or allowance was payable to me for March 1996 or an earlier month`
            `a pension or allowance was payable to the person for the month of January 2001 or an earlier month` IS `a pension or allowance was payable to me for January 2001 or an earlier month`
            `before March 7, 1996 the person was residing in Canada as a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident` IS `before March 7, 1996 I was living in Canada as a citizen or permanent resident`


-- s 12.1(1). An additional amount for a pensioner with no spouse, or whose spouse is paid no benefit. If you are a pensioner whose
-- spouse IS paid a benefit, subsection (1) is silent (fork F-12.1-2) and the answer is blank (NOTHING), not zero; that case falls under (2).
@export How much may be added to my supplement if I have no spouse, or my spouse gets no benefit (s 12.1(1))?
GIVEN `the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? (give any date in that month)
      `the amount determined for A` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the figure for A in section 12.1 for your quarter (the top-up base amount), in dollars?
      `my years of residence in Canada after age 18` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years have you lived in Canada since you turned 18, counted to the last day of the previous month?
      `a pension or allowance was payable to me for March 1996 or an earlier month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a pension or an allowance payable to you for the month of March 1996 or an earlier month?
      `a pension or allowance was payable to me for January 2001 or an earlier month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a pension or an allowance payable to you for the month of January 2001 or an earlier month?
      `before March 7, 1996 I was living in Canada as a citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before March 7, 1996, were you living in Canada as a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident?
      `I have no spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have no spouse or common-law partner?
      `the day before the current payment period I had a spouse or partner to whom no benefit may be paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On the day before the current payment period began, did you have a spouse or common-law partner to whom no benefit may be paid for any month in the period?
      `my income for the base calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your income for the base calendar year, in dollars?
      `our combined income for the base calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your combined income with your spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much may be added to my supplement under section 12.1(1)` IS
    `s 12.1: the amount that may be added, given the amount determined by the formula` (`s 12.1(1): the amount determined by the formula for a pensioner referred to in paragraph 12(1)(a)` `the month I am asking about` `the amount determined for A` `my special qualification facts` `I have no spouse or common-law partner` `the day before the current payment period I had a spouse or partner to whom no benefit may be paid` `my income for the base calendar year` `our combined income for the base calendar year`)
    WHERE
        `my special qualification facts` MEANS `Special qualification facts` WITH
            `years of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age, as of the last day of the immediately preceding month` IS `my years of residence in Canada after age 18`
            `a pension or allowance was payable to the person for the month of March 1996 or an earlier month` IS `a pension or allowance was payable to me for March 1996 or an earlier month`
            `a pension or allowance was payable to the person for the month of January 2001 or an earlier month` IS `a pension or allowance was payable to me for January 2001 or an earlier month`
            `before March 7, 1996 the person was residing in Canada as a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident` IS `before March 7, 1996 I was living in Canada as a citizen or permanent resident`


-- s 12.1(2). The additional amount for a pensioner whose spouse or common-law partner is paid a pension (paragraph 12(1)(b)).
@export How much may be added to my supplement if my spouse also gets a pension (s 12.1(2))?
GIVEN `the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? (give any date in that month)
      `the amount determined for A` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the figure for A in section 12.1 for your quarter (the top-up base amount), in dollars?
      `my years of residence in Canada after age 18` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years have you lived in Canada since you turned 18, counted to the last day of the previous month?
      `a pension or allowance was payable to me for March 1996 or an earlier month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a pension or an allowance payable to you for the month of March 1996 or an earlier month?
      `a pension or allowance was payable to me for January 2001 or an earlier month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a pension or an allowance payable to you for the month of January 2001 or an earlier month?
      `before March 7, 1996 I was living in Canada as a citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before March 7, 1996, were you living in Canada as a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident?
      `our combined income for the base calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your combined income with your spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much may be added to my supplement under section 12.1(2)` IS
    `s 12.1: the amount that may be added, given the amount determined by the formula` (JUST (`s 12.1(2): the amount determined by the formula for a pensioner referred to in paragraph 12(1)(b)` `the month I am asking about` `the amount determined for A` `my special qualification facts` `our combined income for the base calendar year`))
    WHERE
        `my special qualification facts` MEANS `Special qualification facts` WITH
            `years of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age, as of the last day of the immediately preceding month` IS `my years of residence in Canada after age 18`
            `a pension or allowance was payable to the person for the month of March 1996 or an earlier month` IS `a pension or allowance was payable to me for March 1996 or an earlier month`
            `a pension or allowance was payable to the person for the month of January 2001 or an earlier month` IS `a pension or allowance was payable to me for January 2001 or an earlier month`
            `before March 7, 1996 the person was residing in Canada as a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident` IS `before March 7, 1996 I was living in Canada as a citizen or permanent resident`


§§ `My income, and the Minister's estimates (ss 13, 14)`

-- s 14(1). Your application must include a statement of your income for the base calendar year. That is your duty; the Minister's
-- correlative right is to receive it, and the Minister may waive it (s 14(1.01)).
@export Must I state my income for the base calendar year when I apply (s 14(1))?
GIVEN `I am applying for a supplement for the current payment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you applying for a supplement for the current payment period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I state my income for the base calendar year when I apply` IF
    `s 14(1): the person must make a statement of the person's income for the base calendar year in the application` `I am applying for a supplement for the current payment period`


-- s 14(2). If you stop working (or stop running a business) before the current payment period, you may file a statement estimating
-- your income for the year. The statement is due by the end of the second payment period after the one in which you stopped.
-- Your power to file is the Minister's liability to use your estimate.
@export May I file a statement of estimated income because I stopped work (s 14(2))?
GIVEN `I am an applicant, or my spouse or partner is an applicant and has filed a statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you applying for the supplement, or are you the spouse or common-law partner of an applicant who has filed a statement?
      `the month I stopped work` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you stop holding an office or employment, or stop carrying on a business? (give any date in that month)
      `a month in my current payment period` IS A DATE @desc Give any date in the current payment period you are asking about.
      `the day I file the statement` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you file, or will you file, the statement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I file a statement of estimated income because I stopped work` IF
    `s 14(2): the person may file a statement of estimated income` `I am an applicant, or my spouse or partner is an applicant and has filed a statement` `the month I stopped work` `my current payment period` `the day I file the statement`
    WHERE
        `my current payment period` MEANS `s 10: the current payment period` `a month in my current payment period`


-- s 14(2)(a). The estimate is the pension income received, divided by the number of months it covers and multiplied by 12, plus
-- the other income the subsection counts. Blank (NOTHING) if the number of months is zero.
@export What income will be counted if I file a statement of estimated income because I stopped work (s 14(2))?
GIVEN `the month I stopped work` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you stop holding an office or employment, or stop carrying on a business? (give any date in that month)
      `the pension income I received in the period the subsection names` IS A NUMBER @desc What pension income did you receive in the period the subsection names, in dollars?
      `the income from any office, employment or business that the subsection counts` IS A NUMBER @desc What income from an office, employment or business does the subsection count, in dollars?
      `my income for the base year as if I had no such income and no pension income` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your income for the base calendar year, worked out as though you had had no income from an office, employment or business and no pension income, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What income will be counted if I file a statement of estimated income` IS
    `s 14(2): the estimated income` `the month I stopped work` `my figures`
    WHERE
        `my figures` MEANS `s 14: Figures for a statement of estimated income` WITH
            `the pension income received by the person in the period the subsection names` IS `the pension income I received in the period the subsection names`
            `the income from any office or employment or any business that the subsection counts` IS `the income from any office, employment or business that the subsection counts`
            `the person's income for the base calendar year calculated as though, for that year, the person had no income from any office or employment or any business and no pension income` IS `my income for the base year as if I had no such income and no pension income`


-- s 14(7). A supplement calculated on your statement of estimated income may be paid from the month the statement shows.
@export From which month can a supplement calculated on my statement be paid (s 14(7))?
GIVEN `what my statement shows` IS A `s 14(7): What the statement shows` @desc What does your statement of estimated income show: the month you stopped work, or the month you lost pension income?
      `the month shown in my statement` IS A DATE @desc What month does your statement show? (give any date in that month)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From which month can a supplement calculated on my statement be paid` IS
    `s 14(7): the first month for which a supplement calculated on the statement may be paid` `what my statement shows` `the month shown in my statement`


§§ `My spouse or common-law partner (s 15)`

-- s 15(1). Your duty to state your marital situation in the application; the Minister's correlative right is to be told.
@export Must I say in my application whether I have, or had, a spouse or common-law partner (s 15(1))?
GIVEN `I am applying for a supplement for a payment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you applying for a supplement for a payment period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I say in my application whether I have or had a spouse or common-law partner` IF
    `s 15(1): the person must state in the application whether the person has or had a spouse or common-law partner and, if so, who` `I am applying for a supplement for a payment period`


-- s 15(1.1). Where your application was waived, you must tell the Minister without delay if you had no spouse or partner before the
-- last payment period but now have one.
@export Must I tell the Minister without delay that my situation has changed since my last payment period (s 15(1.1))?
GIVEN `the Minister waived my need to apply for the payment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister waive the need for you to apply for the current payment period?
      `I had no spouse or partner before the last payment period for which a supplement was paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have no spouse or common-law partner immediately before the last payment period for which a supplement was paid (or, if none was paid, an application received)?
      `I have a spouse or partner immediately before the current payment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a spouse or common-law partner immediately before the current payment period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I tell the Minister without delay that my situation has changed` IF
    `s 15(1.1): the person must notify the Minister without delay of the change` `the Minister waived my need to apply for the payment period` `I had no spouse or partner before the last payment period for which a supplement was paid` `I have a spouse or partner immediately before the current payment period`


-- s 15(9). Your duty to inform the Minister without delay of a change in your marital situation.
@export Must I tell the Minister without delay if I separate, or lose my spouse or partner (s 15(9))?
GIVEN `I separate from my spouse or partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you separate from a spouse or common-law partner?
      `I cease to have a spouse or partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you cease to have a spouse or common-law partner?
      `I had a spouse or partner at the beginning of a month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a spouse or common-law partner at the beginning of a month?
      `I had no spouse or partner at the beginning of the previous month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have no spouse or common-law partner at the beginning of the previous month?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I tell the Minister without delay if I separate or lose my spouse or partner` IF
    `s 15(9): the applicant must inform the Minister without delay` `I separate from my spouse or partner` `I cease to have a spouse or partner` `I had a spouse or partner at the beginning of a month` `I had no spouse or partner at the beginning of the previous month`


-- s 15(4.1). Where the Minister is satisfied that you are separated, your application is dealt with as though you had no spouse
-- for the months the subsection names; otherwise the answer is blank (NOTHING): other rules of section 15 may still apply.
@export Will my supplement be worked out as though I had, or had no, spouse for a month in which we are separated (s 15(4.1))?
GIVEN `the month the supplement is calculated for` IS A DATE @desc For which month is the supplement calculated? (give any date in that month)
      `the first day of the payment period of my application` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the payment period for which you applied?
      `the Minister is satisfied that we have been separated for at least three months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that you have been separated from your spouse for a continuous period of at least three months, not counting the month you separated?
      `the month we separated` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you and your spouse become separated? (give any date in that month)
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 15: Treatment of the applicant's marital status in the calculation`
DECIDE `Will my supplement be worked out as though I had or had no spouse while we are separated` IS
    `s 15(4.1): the treatment for a separated person` `the month the supplement is calculated for` `the first day of the payment period of my application` `the Minister is satisfied that we have been separated for at least three months` `the month we separated`


-- s 15(7.2). After your common-law partner's death the supplement is worked out as the subsection says; otherwise blank (NOTHING).
@export Will my supplement be worked out as though I had no partner after my common-law partner dies (s 15(7.2))?
GIVEN `the month the supplement is calculated for` IS A DATE @desc For which month is the supplement calculated? (give any date in that month)
      `a month in the payment period of my application` IS A DATE @desc Give any date in the payment period for which you applied.
      `my common-law partner died in the payment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your common-law partner die at a time in the payment period?
      `the month my common-law partner died` IS A DATE @desc In which month did your common-law partner die? (give any date in that month)
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 15: Treatment of the applicant's marital status in the calculation`
DECIDE `Will my supplement be worked out as though I had no partner after my common-law partner dies` IS
    `s 15(7.2): the treatment after a common-law partner dies` `the month the supplement is calculated for` `my payment period` `my common-law partner died in the payment period` `the month my common-law partner died`
    WHERE
        `my payment period` MEANS `s 10: the current payment period` `a month in the payment period of my application`


§§ `Decisions, notices and payment (ss 16 to 18.2)`

-- s 16(1). Your right to have the application considered; the Minister's correlative duty is to consider it without delay.
@export Must the Minister consider my application for the supplement without delay (s 16(1))?
GIVEN `the Minister has received my application for the supplement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister received your application for the supplement?
      `the Minister has waived my need to apply for the supplement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister waived the need for you to apply for the supplement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister consider my application for the supplement without delay` IF
    `s 16(1): the Minister must consider without delay whether the applicant is entitled to be paid a supplement` `the Minister has received my application for the supplement` `the Minister has waived my need to apply for the supplement`


-- s 16(2). Your right to be told the basis of the amount; the Minister's correlative duty is to notify you in writing forthwith.
@export If I ask, will the Minister tell me in writing how my amount was worked out (s 16(2))?
GIVEN `I have asked for particulars of how my supplement was fixed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you asked for particulars of the basis on which the amount of your supplement was fixed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the Minister tell me in writing how my amount was worked out` IF
    `s 16(2): the Minister must forthwith notify the applicant in writing of the basis on which the amount was fixed` `I have asked for particulars of how my supplement was fixed`


-- s 16(2). Your right to be told of the decision and the reasons.
@export Will the Minister tell me in writing why no supplement may be paid to me (s 16(2))?
GIVEN `the Minister has decided that no supplement may be paid to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister decided that no supplement may be paid to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the Minister tell me in writing why no supplement may be paid to me` IF
    `s 16(2): the Minister must forthwith notify the applicant in writing of the decision that no supplement may be paid and the Minister's reasons` `the Minister has decided that no supplement may be paid to me`


-- s 17. Payment is made in arrears at the end of the month, but if payment is approved after the end of the first month payable,
-- payments for that month and the months before it may be made at the end of the month of approval or the month after.
@export What is the earliest day on which payment for this month can be made (s 17)?
GIVEN `the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? (give any date in that month)
      `the first month for which a payment of my supplement may be made` IS A DATE @desc What is the first month for which a payment of your supplement may be made? (give any date in that month)
      `the day payment of my supplement was approved` IS A DATE @desc On what day was payment of your supplement approved?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the earliest day on which payment for this month can be made` IS
    (`s 17: the end-of-month days on which payment for the month may be made` `the month I am asking about` `the first month for which a payment of my supplement may be made` `the day payment of my supplement was approved`)'s `the earliest day`


-- s 17, as above.
@export What is the latest day on which payment for this month can be made (s 17)?
GIVEN `the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? (give any date in that month)
      `the first month for which a payment of my supplement may be made` IS A DATE @desc What is the first month for which a payment of your supplement may be made? (give any date in that month)
      `the day payment of my supplement was approved` IS A DATE @desc On what day was payment of your supplement approved?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the latest day on which payment for this month can be made` IS
    (`s 17: the end-of-month days on which payment for the month may be made` `the month I am asking about` `the first month for which a payment of my supplement may be made` `the day payment of my supplement was approved`)'s `the latest day`


-- s 18(a). If the income you showed was less than your actual income, the Minister deducts and retains the difference out of your
-- later payments (the Minister's power is your liability).
@export How much will be deducted from my later payments if my income turns out to have been higher than I showed (s 18(a))?
GIVEN `my actual income` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your actual income, in dollars?
      `the income I showed` IS A NUMBER @desc What income did you show in your application or statement, in dollars?
      `the supplement I was paid for the months` IS A NUMBER @desc How much supplement was paid to you for the months in the payment period, in dollars?
      `the supplement I would have been paid if I had shown my actual income` IS A NUMBER @desc How much supplement would have been paid to you for those months if the income you showed had been equal to your actual income, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much will be deducted from my later payments if my income was higher than I showed` IS
    `s 18(a): the amount to be deducted and retained out of subsequent payments of supplement or pension` `my actual income` `the income I showed` `the supplement I was paid for the months` `the supplement I would have been paid if I had shown my actual income`


-- s 18(b). Read as the mirror of paragraph (a) (fork F-18-1: read as written, paragraph (b) yields nothing). The Minister's duty
-- to pay is your right.
@export How much will be paid to me if my income turns out to have been lower than I showed (s 18(b))?
GIVEN `my actual income` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your actual income, in dollars?
      `the income I showed` IS A NUMBER @desc What income did you show in your application or statement, in dollars?
      `the supplement I was paid for the months` IS A NUMBER @desc How much supplement was paid to you for the months in the payment period, in dollars?
      `the supplement I would have been paid if I had shown my actual income` IS A NUMBER @desc How much supplement would have been paid to you for those months if the income you showed had been equal to your actual income, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much will be paid to me if my income was lower than I showed` IS
    `s 18(b): the amount to be paid to the applicant, read as the mirror of paragraph (a)` `my actual income` `the income I showed` `the supplement I was paid for the months` `the supplement I would have been paid if I had shown my actual income`


-- s 18.1. You may ask in writing that your supplement cease to be payable; it then ceases on the last day of the month of approval.
@export On what day does my supplement stop if I ask the Minister in writing to stop it (s 18.1)?
GIVEN `the month the Minister approved my request` IS A DATE @desc In which month did the Minister approve your request? (give any date in that month)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day does my supplement stop if I ask the Minister to stop it` IS
    `s 18.1: the last day of the month on which the supplement ceases to be payable` `the month the Minister approved my request`


-- s 18.1. After you ask for the supplement to stop you may apply again; it may resume from the month you choose, no earlier than the month
-- the new application is received.
@export From which month can my supplement start again after I asked for it to stop (s 18.1)?
GIVEN `the month the Minister received my new application` IS A DATE @desc In which month did the Minister receive your new application? (give any date in that month)
      `the month I chose in the application` IS A DATE @desc Which month did you choose in the application? (give any date in that month)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From which month can my supplement start again after I asked for it to stop` IS
    `s 18.1: the first month in which the supplement may resume` `the month the Minister received my new application` `the month I chose in the application`


-- s 18.1. Your supplement is not payable between the month your request is approved and the month it may resume.
@export Can my supplement still be paid for this month although I asked for it to stop (s 18.1)?
GIVEN `the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? (give any date in that month)
      `I have asked the Minister in writing that my supplement stop` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you asked the Minister in writing that your supplement cease to be payable?
      `the month the Minister approved my request` IS A DATE @desc In which month did the Minister approve your request? (give any date in that month)
      `the first month my supplement may resume` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc What is the first month in which your supplement may resume? (leave blank if you have not applied again)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my supplement still be paid for this month although I asked for it to stop` IF
    `s 18.1: the supplement is payable for the month in spite of the request` `the month I am asking about` `I have asked the Minister in writing that my supplement stop` `the month the Minister approved my request` `the first month my supplement may resume`


-- s 18.2(1). Your power to ask that your application for the supplement be treated as never made, in the prescribed manner and within the prescribed time after payment
-- began. Both are set by Regulation 26.1(1) (piece oa3): the request is made to the Minister in writing, no later than six months after the day payment begins.
-- The figure and the manner are taken from that Regulation here, in the seat only; the layer-1 rule keeps them as inputs.
@export May I ask for my supplement to be cancelled after payment has started (s 18.2(1))?
GIVEN `I make the request to the Minister in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make the request to the Minister in writing?
      `the day payment of my supplement began` IS A DATE @desc On what day did payment of your supplement begin?
      `the day I make the request` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you make the request?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask for my supplement to be cancelled after payment has started` IF
    `s 18.2(1): the pensioner may request cancellation of the supplement` `I make the request to the Minister in writing` `the day payment of my supplement began` (`a limit in months` 6) `the day I make the request`


§ `Old Age Security Act -- Part III: the Allowances, for a person 60 to 64`

§§ `Allowance for the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner (ss 19, 20)`

-- s 19. An Allowance may be paid to the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner who is 60 to 64, resident in Canada, and not
-- barred by one of the limitations of subsection (6). The pensioner's side of the relation (whether a supplement could be paid to
-- the pensioner, whether the pensioner is incarcerated, whether you made a joint application) is taken as facts you can state.
-- Fixed value: the month in which you die is left blank, because you are asking about your own entitlement while living.
@export May I be paid an Allowance for this month as the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner (s 19)?
GIVEN `the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? (give any date in that month)
      `my relation to the pensioner` IS A `s 19(1): Relation to the pensioner` @desc Are you the pensioner's spouse, the pensioner's common-law partner, or a former common-law partner of the pensioner?
      `I am separated from the pensioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you separated from the pensioner?
      `the sole reason we are separated is that one of us is incarcerated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sole reason for the separation that one of you is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3) or paragraph 19(6)(f) of the Act?
      `the sole reason we are separated is that the pensioner is incarcerated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sole reason for the separation that the pensioner is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3) of the Act?
      `the day our separation began` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day did the separation begin? (leave blank if you are not separated)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `my years of residence in Canada since age 18` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many years in total have you resided in Canada after turning 18, counted up to the day before your application was approved?
      `I was resident in Canada on the day before my application was approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you resident in Canada on the day before your application was approved?
      `I was a Canadian citizen on the day before my application was approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a Canadian citizen on the day before your application for an allowance was approved?
      `I was legally resident in Canada on the day before my application was approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you legally resident in Canada on the day before your application for an allowance was approved?
      `I was a Canadian citizen on the day before I stopped residing in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a Canadian citizen on the day before you ceased to reside in Canada?
      `I was legally resident in Canada on the day before I stopped residing in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you legally resident in Canada on the day before you ceased to reside in Canada?
      `the pensioner and I made a joint application for the payment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you and the pensioner make a joint application for an allowance for the payment period?
      `an application described in section 30 has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application described in section 30 of the Act been made?
      `the pensioner is incarcerated and I have applied individually` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the pensioner an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3) of the Act, and have you applied for the allowance individually?
      `payment of my allowance has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has payment of your allowance been approved?
      `the Minister waived my need to apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister waive the need for you to apply for the allowance under subsection 19(4.1)?
      `the month my application was received, treated as made, or waived` IS A DATE @desc In which month was your application received, treated as made, or waived? (give any date in that month)
      `no supplement may be paid to the pensioner for the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is no supplement payable to the pensioner for the month you are asking about?
      `a supplement would be payable to the pensioner if the pensioner's special qualifying factor were one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would a supplement be payable to the pensioner for the month if the pensioner's special qualifying factor were equal to one?
      `a supplement would be payable to the pensioner if subsection 5(3) did not bar it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would a supplement be payable to the pensioner for the month if the pensioner were not precluded from receiving one by subsection 5(3) of the Act?
      `I am out of Canada for the whole month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you out of Canada for the whole of the month you are asking about?
      `the month I left Canada` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc In which month did you leave Canada? (leave blank if you have not left)
      `I have stayed outside Canada since I left` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you stayed outside Canada ever since you left?
      `a sponsor's undertaking is in effect for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a sponsor's undertaking under the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act in effect in respect of you during the month?
      `I was qualified for an allowance just before paragraph 19(6)(d) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you qualified to receive an allowance immediately before the day on which paragraph 19(6)(d) of the Act came into force?
      `an event described in the regulations has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an event happened that the Old Age Security Regulations say lifts the limit on sponsored persons?
      `I am a common-law partner who was not a spouse when paragraph 19(6)(e) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a common-law partner who was not a spouse immediately before the coming into force of paragraph 19(6)(e) of the Act?
      `the month paragraph 19(6)(e) came into force` IS A DATE @desc In which month did paragraph 19(6)(e) of the Act come into force? (the text does not give it; give any date in that month)
      `I am subject to a sentence of imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to a sentence of imprisonment?
      `my sentence is to be served in a penitentiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your sentence to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament?
      `the length of my sentence in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How long is your sentence of imprisonment, in days?
      `my sentence is to be served in a prison under the Prisons and Reformatories Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your sentence to be served in a prison, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Prisons and Reformatories Act?
      `the province has an agreement under section 41` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the government of the province in which the prison is located entered into an agreement under section 41 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act?
      `the first day of my period of incarceration` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day did your period of incarceration begin? (leave blank if you are not incarcerated)
      `the month I am released` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc In which month are you, or were you, released? (leave blank if you have not been)
      `I have notified the Minister in writing of my release` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you notified the Minister in writing, before or after your release?
      `the month I became the spouse or partner of another person` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc In which month did you become the spouse or common-law partner of another person? (leave blank if you have not)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be paid an Allowance for this month as the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` IF
    `s 19: an allowance may be paid to the person for the month` `the month I am asking about` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 19: Facts about a person who may be paid an allowance and a month` WITH
            `the relation of the person to the pensioner` IS `my relation to the pensioner`
            `the person is separated from the pensioner` IS `I am separated from the pensioner`
            `the sole reason for the separation is that one of the partners is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3) or paragraph 19(6)(f)` IS `the sole reason we are separated is that one of us is incarcerated`
            `the sole reason for the separation is that the pensioner is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` IS `the sole reason we are separated is that the pensioner is incarcerated`
            `the day on which the separation commenced` IS `the day our separation began`
            `the person's date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `the aggregate period of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which the application is approved, in years` IS `my years of residence in Canada since age 18`
            `the person was resident in Canada on the day preceding the day on which the application is approved` IS `I was resident in Canada on the day before my application was approved`
            `on the day preceding the day on which the application for an allowance is approved the person is a Canadian citizen` IS `I was a Canadian citizen on the day before my application was approved`
            `on the day preceding the day on which the application for an allowance is approved the person is legally resident in Canada` IS `I was legally resident in Canada on the day before my application was approved`
            `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada the person was a Canadian citizen` IS `I was a Canadian citizen on the day before I stopped residing in Canada`
            `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada the person was legally resident in Canada` IS `I was legally resident in Canada on the day before I stopped residing in Canada`
            `a joint application of the pensioner and the person has been made for the payment period` IS `the pensioner and I made a joint application for the payment period`
            `an application described in section 30 has been made` IS `an application described in section 30 has been made`
            `the pensioner is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3) and the person has applied individually` IS `the pensioner is incarcerated and I have applied individually`
            `payment of the allowance has been approved under this Part` IS `payment of my allowance has been approved`
            `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 19(4.1)` IS `the Minister waived my need to apply`
            `the month in which the application is received or is deemed to have been made or in which the requirement for an application has been waived` IS `the month my application was received, treated as made, or waived`
            `no supplement may be paid to the pensioner for the month` IS `no supplement may be paid to the pensioner for the month`
            `a supplement would be payable to the pensioner for the month if the pensioner's special qualifying factor were equal to one` IS `a supplement would be payable to the pensioner if the pensioner's special qualifying factor were one`
            `a supplement would be payable to the pensioner for the month if the pensioner were not precluded from receiving a supplement by subsection 5(3)` IS `a supplement would be payable to the pensioner if subsection 5(3) did not bar it`
            `the person is absent from Canada throughout the month` IS `I am out of Canada for the whole month`
            `the month in which the person left Canada` IS `the month I left Canada`
            `the person has remained outside Canada since leaving` IS `I have stayed outside Canada since I left`
            `an undertaking by a sponsor is in effect in respect of the person` IS `a sponsor's undertaking is in effect for me`
            `the person was qualified to receive an allowance immediately before the day on which paragraph 19(6)(d) came into force` IS `I was qualified for an allowance just before paragraph 19(6)(d) came into force`
            `an event as provided by the regulations has occurred` IS `an event described in the regulations has occurred`
            `the person is a common-law partner who was not a spouse immediately before the coming into force of paragraph 19(6)(e)` IS `I am a common-law partner who was not a spouse when paragraph 19(6)(e) came into force`
            `the month in which paragraph 19(6)(e) comes into force` IS `the month paragraph 19(6)(e) came into force`
            `the sentence of imprisonment the person is subject to` IS `my sentence`
            `the first day of the period of incarceration` IS `the first day of my period of incarceration`
            `the month in which the person is released` IS `the month I am released`
            `the person has notified the Minister in writing before or after the release` IS `I have notified the Minister in writing of my release`
            `the month in which the person dies` IS NOTHING
            `the month in which the person becomes the spouse or common-law partner of another person` IS `the month I became the spouse or partner of another person`
        `my sentence` MEANS
            IF `I am subject to a sentence of imprisonment`
            THEN JUST (`Sentence of imprisonment` WITH
                           `to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` IS `my sentence is to be served in a penitentiary`
                           `length in days` IS `the length of my sentence in days`
                           `to be served in a prison as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Prisons and Reformatories Act` IS `my sentence is to be served in a prison under the Prisons and Reformatories Act`
                           `the government of the province in which the prison is located has entered into an agreement under section 41 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act` IS `the province has an agreement under section 41`)
            ELSE NOTHING


-- s 19(4.2). If the Minister waived your application for a payment period, the Minister may notify you in writing that you must apply for
-- later months, not later than fifteen days before the first of them.
@export By what day may the Minister notify me that I must apply for later months of the Allowance (s 19(4.2))?
GIVEN `the first of the months for which I must apply` IS A DATE @desc What is the first month for which you must apply? (give any date in that month)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day may the Minister notify me that I must apply for later months of the Allowance` IS
    `s 19(4.2): the last day on which the Minister may give the notice` `the first of the months for which I must apply`


-- ss 19(7), 22(3). The Allowance depends on the pension equivalent, the supplement equivalent, your special qualifying factor and the
-- monthly joint income of you and the pensioner (one-twelfth of both incomes for the base year, or only yours in a month the definition names).
@export How much Allowance may I be paid for this month as the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner (ss 19(7), 22(3))?
GIVEN `the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? (give any date in that month)
      `the full monthly pension for the month, not increased under subsection 7(5)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the full monthly pension payable for the month under section 7, not increased under subsection 7(5), in dollars?
      `the supplement equivalent for the month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the supplement equivalent for the month, in dollars?
      `my years of residence in Canada after age 18` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years have you lived in Canada since you turned 18, counted to the last day of the previous month?
      `a pension or allowance was payable to me for March 1996 or an earlier month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a pension or an allowance payable to you for the month of March 1996 or an earlier month?
      `a pension or allowance was payable to me for January 2001 or an earlier month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a pension or an allowance payable to you for the month of January 2001 or an earlier month?
      `before March 7, 1996 I was living in Canada as a citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before March 7, 1996, were you living in Canada as a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident?
      `the pensioner's income for the base calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the pensioner's income for the base calendar year, in dollars?
      `my income for the base calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your own income for the base calendar year, in dollars?
      `the pensioner is incarcerated (paragraph (a) of the definition)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the pensioner an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3) of the Act?
      `the first month of the pensioner's incarceration` IS A DATE @desc In which month did the pensioner's incarceration begin? (give any date; ignored if the pensioner is not incarcerated)
      `the month the pensioner is released` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc In which month is the pensioner released? (leave blank if not yet released or not incarcerated)
      `a direction under subsection 19(8) is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a direction made under subsection 19(8) in respect of you in effect (not cancelled under subsection 19(9))?
      `I am not living with the pensioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not living with the pensioner in a dwelling maintained by one or the other of you?
      `the first month I was not living with the pensioner` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you first stop living with the pensioner? (give any date; ignored if you live with the pensioner)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much Allowance may I be paid for this month as the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` IS
    `s 19(7): the amount of the allowance` (`s 22(1): the pension equivalent` `the full monthly pension for the month, not increased under subsection 7(5)`) `the supplement equivalent for the month` (`the special qualifying factor of a person for the month containing` `the month I am asking about` `my special qualification facts`) `our monthly joint income`
    WHERE
        `my special qualification facts` MEANS `Special qualification facts` WITH
            `years of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age, as of the last day of the immediately preceding month` IS `my years of residence in Canada after age 18`
            `a pension or allowance was payable to the person for the month of March 1996 or an earlier month` IS `a pension or allowance was payable to me for March 1996 or an earlier month`
            `a pension or allowance was payable to the person for the month of January 2001 or an earlier month` IS `a pension or allowance was payable to me for January 2001 or an earlier month`
            `before March 7, 1996 the person was residing in Canada as a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident` IS `before March 7, 1996 I was living in Canada as a citizen or permanent resident`
        `our monthly joint income` MEANS
            `s 22(1): the monthly joint income` `the pensioner's income for the base calendar year` `my income for the base calendar year` `the month is one of the months in paragraph (a) or (b)`
        `the month is one of the months in paragraph (a) or (b)` MEANS
                `s 22(1) "monthly joint income" (a): the month is one in which the pensioner is incarcerated, exclusive of the first month and the month of release` `the month I am asking about` `the pensioner is incarcerated (paragraph (a) of the definition)` `the first month of the pensioner's incarceration` `the month the pensioner is released`
            OR  `s 22(1) "monthly joint income" (b): the month is one in which the spouse or common-law partner is not living with the pensioner, exclusive of the first month` `the month I am asking about` `a direction under subsection 19(8) is in effect` `I am not living with the pensioner` `the first month I was not living with the pensioner`


-- s 20. The Minister may suspend payment of your Allowance if you do not comply (the Minister's power is your liability).
@export May payment of my Allowance be suspended if I do not comply with the Act (s 20)?
GIVEN `I fail to comply with a provision of the Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fail to comply with a provision of the Act or the Old Age Security Regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May payment of my Allowance be suspended if I do not comply with the Act` IF
    `s 20: payment of an allowance may be suspended` `I fail to comply with a provision of the Act or the regulations`


-- s 20. Payment resumes once you comply.
@export May payment of my suspended Allowance be resumed (s 20)?
GIVEN `payment of my Allowance has been suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has payment of your Allowance been suspended under section 20?
      `I now comply with the provisions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you now comply with the provisions of the Act and the regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May payment of my suspended Allowance be resumed` IF
    `s 20: payment of the allowance may be resumed` `payment of my Allowance has been suspended` `I now comply with the provisions`


-- s 19(8). The Minister's power to direct; the correlative liability is yours.
@export May the Minister work out my Allowance without counting the pensioner's income because we do not live together (s 19(8))?
GIVEN `I have applied for an Allowance for the payment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for an Allowance for the payment period?
      `the Minister is satisfied that we were not living together through no fault of ours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that, for reasons not attributable to you or the pensioner, you were not living with the pensioner in a dwelling maintained by one or the other of you when you applied?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Minister work out my Allowance without counting the pensioner's income` IF
    `s 19(8): the Minister may direct that the monthly joint income be determined without the pensioner's income` `I have applied for an Allowance for the payment period` `the Minister is satisfied that we were not living together through no fault of ours`


§§ `Allowance for a survivor (ss 21, 21.1)`

-- s 21. A survivor aged 60 to 64 whose spouse or common-law partner has died may be paid an Allowance, subject to the residence
-- test, an approved application and the limitations of subsection (9). Section 21.1 (a conviction for killing the spouse) is a
-- separate question below. Fixed value: the month in which you die is left blank, because you are asking about your own
-- entitlement while living.
@export May I be paid an Allowance for this month as a survivor (s 21)?
GIVEN `the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? (give any date in that month)
      `my spouse or common-law partner has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your spouse or common-law partner died?
      `I have since become the spouse or partner of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you since become the spouse or common-law partner of another person?
      `the month I became a survivor` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you become a survivor (the month your spouse or common-law partner died)? (give any date in that month)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `my years of residence in Canada since age 18` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many years in total have you resided in Canada after turning 18, counted up to the day before your application was approved?
      `I was resident in Canada on the day before my application was approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you resident in Canada on the day before your application was approved?
      `I was a Canadian citizen on the day before my application was approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a Canadian citizen on the day before your application for an allowance was approved?
      `I was legally resident in Canada on the day before my application was approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you legally resident in Canada on the day before your application for an allowance was approved?
      `I was a Canadian citizen on the day before I stopped residing in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a Canadian citizen on the day before you ceased to reside in Canada?
      `I was legally resident in Canada on the day before I stopped residing in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you legally resident in Canada on the day before you ceased to reside in Canada?
      `I have applied for the Allowance for the payment period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for an allowance for the payment period?
      `payment of my Allowance has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has payment of your allowance been approved?
      `my spouse and I made a joint application before the pensioner's death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you and the pensioner make a joint application for an allowance under section 19, before the pensioner's death, for months in the payment period of the death or the following payment period, and is this a payment period for which it was made?
      `the Minister waived my need to apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Minister waive the need for you to apply for the allowance under subsection 21(5.1)?
      `the month my application was received, treated as made, or waived` IS A DATE @desc In which month was your application received, treated as made, or waived? (give any date in that month)
      `I was not a widow when subsection 21(7.1) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a survivor who was not a widow immediately before the coming into force of subsection 21(7.1) of the Act?
      `the day I became a survivor` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you become a survivor?
      `the month subsection 21(7.1) came into force` IS A DATE @desc In which month did subsection 21(7.1) of the Act come into force? (the text does not give it; give any date in that month)
      `I am out of Canada for the whole month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you out of Canada for the whole of the month you are asking about?
      `the month I left Canada` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc In which month did you leave Canada? (leave blank if you have not left)
      `I have stayed outside Canada since I left` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you stayed outside Canada ever since you left?
      `a sponsor's undertaking is in effect for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a sponsor's undertaking under the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act in effect in respect of you during the month?
      `I was qualified for an allowance just before paragraph 21(9)(c) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you qualified to receive an allowance immediately before the day on which paragraph 21(9)(c) of the Act came into force?
      `an event described in the regulations has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an event happened that the Old Age Security Regulations say lifts the limit on sponsored persons?
      `I am subject to a sentence of imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to a sentence of imprisonment?
      `my sentence is to be served in a penitentiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your sentence to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament?
      `the length of my sentence in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How long is your sentence of imprisonment, in days?
      `my sentence is to be served in a prison under the Prisons and Reformatories Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your sentence to be served in a prison, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Prisons and Reformatories Act?
      `the province has an agreement under section 41` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the government of the province in which the prison is located entered into an agreement under section 41 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act?
      `the first day of my period of incarceration` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what day did your period of incarceration begin? (leave blank if you are not incarcerated)
      `the month I am released` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc In which month are you, or were you, released? (leave blank if you have not been)
      `I have notified the Minister in writing of my release` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you notified the Minister in writing, before or after your release?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be paid an Allowance for this month as a survivor` IF
    `s 21: an allowance may be paid to the survivor for the month` `the month I am asking about` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month` WITH
            `the person's spouse or common-law partner has died` IS `my spouse or common-law partner has died`
            `the person has since become the spouse or common-law partner of another person` IS `I have since become the spouse or partner of another person`
            `the month in which the person became a survivor` IS `the month I became a survivor`
            `the person's date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `the aggregate period of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which the application is approved, in years` IS `my years of residence in Canada since age 18`
            `the person was resident in Canada on the day preceding the day on which the application is approved` IS `I was resident in Canada on the day before my application was approved`
            `on the day preceding the day on which the application for an allowance is approved the person is a Canadian citizen` IS `I was a Canadian citizen on the day before my application was approved`
            `on the day preceding the day on which the application for an allowance is approved the person is legally resident in Canada` IS `I was legally resident in Canada on the day before my application was approved`
            `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada the person was a Canadian citizen` IS `I was a Canadian citizen on the day before I stopped residing in Canada`
            `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada the person was legally resident in Canada` IS `I was legally resident in Canada on the day before I stopped residing in Canada`
            `the survivor has made an application for an allowance in respect of the payment period` IS `I have applied for the Allowance for the payment period`
            `payment of the allowance has been approved under this Part` IS `payment of my Allowance has been approved`
            `the spouses or common-law partners made a joint application for an allowance under section 19 before the pensioner's death for months in the payment period of the death or the following payment period, and the payment period is one in respect of which it was made` IS `my spouse and I made a joint application before the pensioner's death`
            `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 21(5.1)` IS `the Minister waived my need to apply`
            `the month in which the application is received or is deemed to have been made or in which the requirement for an application has been waived` IS `the month my application was received, treated as made, or waived`
            `the person was not a widow immediately before the coming into force of subsection 21(7.1)` IS `I was not a widow when subsection 21(7.1) came into force`
            `the day on which the person became a survivor` IS `the day I became a survivor`
            `the month in which subsection 21(7.1) comes into force` IS `the month subsection 21(7.1) came into force`
            `the person is absent from Canada throughout the month` IS `I am out of Canada for the whole month`
            `the month in which the person left Canada` IS `the month I left Canada`
            `the person has remained outside Canada since leaving` IS `I have stayed outside Canada since I left`
            `an undertaking by a sponsor is in effect in respect of the person` IS `a sponsor's undertaking is in effect for me`
            `the person was qualified to receive an allowance immediately before the day on which paragraph 21(9)(c) came into force` IS `I was qualified for an allowance just before paragraph 21(9)(c) came into force`
            `an event as provided by the regulations has occurred` IS `an event described in the regulations has occurred`
            `the sentence of imprisonment the person is subject to` IS `my sentence`
            `the first day of the period of incarceration` IS `the first day of my period of incarceration`
            `the month in which the person is released` IS `the month I am released`
            `the person has notified the Minister in writing before or after the release` IS `I have notified the Minister in writing of my release`
            `the month in which the person dies` IS NOTHING
        `my sentence` MEANS
            IF `I am subject to a sentence of imprisonment`
            THEN JUST (`Sentence of imprisonment` WITH
                           `to be served in a penitentiary by virtue of an Act of Parliament` IS `my sentence is to be served in a penitentiary`
                           `length in days` IS `the length of my sentence in days`
                           `to be served in a prison as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Prisons and Reformatories Act` IS `my sentence is to be served in a prison under the Prisons and Reformatories Act`
                           `the government of the province in which the prison is located has entered into an agreement under section 41 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act` IS `the province has an agreement under section 41`)
            ELSE NOTHING


-- s 21(6). The Allowance may be paid from the month after the month you become a survivor or attain sixty, whichever is later.
-- Placeholder: the rule called reads only the month you became a survivor and your date of birth (the month argument it is given is
-- not read); every other field of the record is given a fixed value.
@export From which month may a survivor's Allowance be paid to me (s 21(6))?
GIVEN `the month I became a survivor` IS A DATE @desc In which month did you become a survivor? (give any date in that month)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From which month may a survivor's Allowance be paid to me` IS
    `s 21(6): the first month for which an allowance may be paid` `the month I became a survivor` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `s 21: Facts about a survivor and a month` WITH
            `the person's spouse or common-law partner has died` IS FALSE
            `the person has since become the spouse or common-law partner of another person` IS FALSE
            `the month in which the person became a survivor` IS `the month I became a survivor`
            `the person's date of birth` IS `my date of birth`
            `the aggregate period of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which the application is approved, in years` IS 0
            `the person was resident in Canada on the day preceding the day on which the application is approved` IS FALSE
            `on the day preceding the day on which the application for an allowance is approved the person is a Canadian citizen` IS FALSE
            `on the day preceding the day on which the application for an allowance is approved the person is legally resident in Canada` IS FALSE
            `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada the person was a Canadian citizen` IS FALSE
            `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada the person was legally resident in Canada` IS FALSE
            `the survivor has made an application for an allowance in respect of the payment period` IS FALSE
            `payment of the allowance has been approved under this Part` IS FALSE
            `the spouses or common-law partners made a joint application for an allowance under section 19 before the pensioner's death for months in the payment period of the death or the following payment period, and the payment period is one in respect of which it was made` IS FALSE
            `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 21(5.1)` IS FALSE
            `the month in which the application is received or is deemed to have been made or in which the requirement for an application has been waived` IS YMD 2000 1 1
            `the person was not a widow immediately before the coming into force of subsection 21(7.1)` IS FALSE
            `the day on which the person became a survivor` IS YMD 2000 1 1
            `the month in which subsection 21(7.1) comes into force` IS YMD 2000 1 1
            `the person is absent from Canada throughout the month` IS FALSE
            `the month in which the person left Canada` IS NOTHING
            `the person has remained outside Canada since leaving` IS FALSE
            `an undertaking by a sponsor is in effect in respect of the person` IS FALSE
            `the person was qualified to receive an allowance immediately before the day on which paragraph 21(9)(c) came into force` IS FALSE
            `an event as provided by the regulations has occurred` IS FALSE
            `the sentence of imprisonment the person is subject to` IS NOTHING
            `the first day of the period of incarceration` IS NOTHING
            `the month in which the person is released` IS NOTHING
            `the person has notified the Minister in writing before or after the release` IS FALSE
            `the month in which the person dies` IS NOTHING


-- s 21(5.2). If the Minister waived your application for some months, the Minister must notify you in writing, not later than fifteen
-- days before the first month for which an application is required.
@export By what day may the Minister notify me that I must apply for later months of the survivor's Allowance (s 21(5.2))?
GIVEN `the first of the subsequent months for which I must apply` IS A DATE @desc What is the first of the later months for which you must apply? (give any date in that month)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day may the Minister notify me that I must apply for later months of the survivor's Allowance` IS
    `s 21(5.2): the last day on which the Minister may give the notice` `the first of the subsequent months for which I must apply`


-- ss 21(10), 22(4). A survivor's Allowance depends on the pension equivalent, the supplement equivalent for a survivor, your special
-- qualifying factor and your monthly income (one-twelfth of your income for the base calendar year).
@export How much Allowance may I be paid for this month as a survivor (ss 21(10), 22(4))?
GIVEN `the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? (give any date in that month)
      `the full monthly pension for the month, not increased under subsection 7(5)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the full monthly pension payable for the month under section 7, not increased under subsection 7(5), in dollars?
      `the supplement equivalent for a survivor for the month` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the supplement equivalent for a survivor for the month, in dollars?
      `my years of residence in Canada after age 18` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years have you lived in Canada since you turned 18, counted to the last day of the previous month?
      `a pension or allowance was payable to me for March 1996 or an earlier month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a pension or an allowance payable to you for the month of March 1996 or an earlier month?
      `a pension or allowance was payable to me for January 2001 or an earlier month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a pension or an allowance payable to you for the month of January 2001 or an earlier month?
      `before March 7, 1996 I was living in Canada as a citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before March 7, 1996, were you living in Canada as a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident?
      `my income for the base calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your income for the base calendar year, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much Allowance may I be paid for this month as a survivor` IS
    `s 21(10): the amount of the allowance` (`s 22(1): the pension equivalent` `the full monthly pension for the month, not increased under subsection 7(5)`) `the supplement equivalent for a survivor for the month` (`the special qualifying factor of a person for the month containing` `the month I am asking about` `my special qualification facts`) (`s 22(1): the monthly income of a survivor` `my income for the base calendar year`)
    WHERE
        `my special qualification facts` MEANS `Special qualification facts` WITH
            `years of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age, as of the last day of the immediately preceding month` IS `my years of residence in Canada after age 18`
            `a pension or allowance was payable to the person for the month of March 1996 or an earlier month` IS `a pension or allowance was payable to me for March 1996 or an earlier month`
            `a pension or allowance was payable to the person for the month of January 2001 or an earlier month` IS `a pension or allowance was payable to me for January 2001 or an earlier month`
            `before March 7, 1996 the person was residing in Canada as a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident` IS `before March 7, 1996 I was living in Canada as a citizen or permanent resident`


-- s 21.1(1), (2), (3), (8). The Allowance is not payable to a person the Minister is informed and satisfied was convicted of murder or
-- manslaughter of the spouse or partner. A foreign conviction counts only if the Minister deems it to; manslaughter with release on a
-- probation order is excepted; and a reversed, withdrawn or stayed conviction no longer bars, once all appeals are exhausted.
@export Is a survivor's Allowance not payable to me because I have been convicted of killing my spouse or partner (s 21.1(1))?
GIVEN `the Minister is informed and satisfied that I was convicted of murder or manslaughter of my spouse or partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister been informed, and is the Minister satisfied, that you have been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of your spouse or common-law partner?
      `my conviction is by a court outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the conviction by a court outside Canada?
      `the Minister has deemed my conviction to be a conviction of murder or manslaughter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister deemed the conviction by a court outside Canada to be a conviction of first or second degree murder or manslaughter?
      `my conviction is for manslaughter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the conviction for manslaughter?
      `I am released on the conditions of a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you released on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under paragraph 731(1)(a) of the Criminal Code?
      `my conviction has been reversed, the charges withdrawn or the proceedings stayed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the conviction has been reversed, the charges have been withdrawn, or the proceedings were stayed and not recommenced within the required time?
      `all rights of appeal have been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all rights of appeal been exhausted?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a survivor's Allowance not payable to me because of a conviction` IF
    `s 21.1(1): an allowance under section 21 is not payable to the individual` `my conviction`
    WHERE
        `my conviction` MEANS `s 21.1: Facts about a conviction` WITH
            `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the spouse or common-law partner` IS `the Minister is informed and satisfied that I was convicted of murder or manslaughter of my spouse or partner`
            `the conviction is by a court outside Canada` IS `my conviction is by a court outside Canada`
            `the Minister has deemed the conviction to be a conviction of first or second degree murder or manslaughter` IS `the Minister has deemed my conviction to be a conviction of murder or manslaughter`
            `the conviction is for manslaughter` IS `my conviction is for manslaughter`
            `the individual is released on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under paragraph 731(1)(a) of the Criminal Code` IS `I am released on the conditions of a probation order`
            `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the conviction has been reversed, the charges have been withdrawn or the proceedings were stayed and not recommenced within the required time period` IS `my conviction has been reversed, the charges withdrawn or the proceedings stayed`
            `all rights of appeal have been exhausted` IS `all rights of appeal have been exhausted`


-- s 21.1(4). A person who received an Allowance and is later found convicted is deemed not to have been entitled, and the amounts are a
-- debt due to the Crown that the Minister must recover (a liability of yours; the Minister's power to recover is the correlative).
@export Must I repay an Allowance I received if I am found to have been convicted of killing my spouse or partner (s 21.1(4))?
GIVEN `I have received an Allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received an Allowance under section 21?
      `the Minister is informed and satisfied that I was convicted of murder or manslaughter of my spouse or partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister been informed, and is the Minister satisfied, that you have been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of your spouse or common-law partner?
      `my conviction is by a court outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the conviction by a court outside Canada?
      `the Minister has deemed my conviction to be a conviction of murder or manslaughter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister deemed the conviction by a court outside Canada to be a conviction of first or second degree murder or manslaughter?
      `my conviction is for manslaughter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the conviction for manslaughter?
      `I am released on the conditions of a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you released on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under paragraph 731(1)(a) of the Criminal Code?
      `my conviction has been reversed, the charges withdrawn or the proceedings stayed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the conviction has been reversed, the charges have been withdrawn, or the proceedings were stayed and not recommenced within the required time?
      `all rights of appeal have been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all rights of appeal been exhausted?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I repay an Allowance I received if I am found to have been convicted` IF
    `s 21.1(4): the person is deemed not to have been entitled and the amounts are a debt that the Minister must recover` `I have received an Allowance` `my conviction`
    WHERE
        `my conviction` MEANS `s 21.1: Facts about a conviction` WITH
            `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the spouse or common-law partner` IS `the Minister is informed and satisfied that I was convicted of murder or manslaughter of my spouse or partner`
            `the conviction is by a court outside Canada` IS `my conviction is by a court outside Canada`
            `the Minister has deemed the conviction to be a conviction of first or second degree murder or manslaughter` IS `the Minister has deemed my conviction to be a conviction of murder or manslaughter`
            `the conviction is for manslaughter` IS `my conviction is for manslaughter`
            `the individual is released on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under paragraph 731(1)(a) of the Criminal Code` IS `I am released on the conditions of a probation order`
            `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the conviction has been reversed, the charges have been withdrawn or the proceedings were stayed and not recommenced within the required time period` IS `my conviction has been reversed, the charges withdrawn or the proceedings stayed`
            `all rights of appeal have been exhausted` IS `all rights of appeal have been exhausted`


-- s 21.1(2). Once the conviction is reversed, the charges withdrawn or the proceedings stayed, and all appeals are exhausted, subsection
-- (1) is treated as never having applied and any amount recovered must be repaid to you.
@export Will the Minister repay what was recovered from me if my conviction is reversed (s 21.1(2))?
GIVEN `an amount has been recovered from me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an amount been recovered from you?
      `the Minister is informed and satisfied that I was convicted of murder or manslaughter of my spouse or partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister been informed, and is the Minister satisfied, that you have been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of your spouse or common-law partner?
      `my conviction is by a court outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the conviction by a court outside Canada?
      `the Minister has deemed my conviction to be a conviction of murder or manslaughter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister deemed the conviction by a court outside Canada to be a conviction of first or second degree murder or manslaughter?
      `my conviction is for manslaughter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the conviction for manslaughter?
      `I am released on the conditions of a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you released on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under paragraph 731(1)(a) of the Criminal Code?
      `my conviction has been reversed, the charges withdrawn or the proceedings stayed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the conviction has been reversed, the charges have been withdrawn, or the proceedings were stayed and not recommenced within the required time?
      `all rights of appeal have been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all rights of appeal been exhausted?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the Minister repay what was recovered from me if my conviction is reversed` IF
    `s 21.1(2): the Minister must repay any amount recovered from the person` `an amount has been recovered from me` `my conviction`
    WHERE
        `my conviction` MEANS `s 21.1: Facts about a conviction` WITH
            `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the individual has been convicted of first or second degree murder or manslaughter of the spouse or common-law partner` IS `the Minister is informed and satisfied that I was convicted of murder or manslaughter of my spouse or partner`
            `the conviction is by a court outside Canada` IS `my conviction is by a court outside Canada`
            `the Minister has deemed the conviction to be a conviction of first or second degree murder or manslaughter` IS `the Minister has deemed my conviction to be a conviction of murder or manslaughter`
            `the conviction is for manslaughter` IS `my conviction is for manslaughter`
            `the individual is released on the conditions prescribed in a probation order under paragraph 731(1)(a) of the Criminal Code` IS `I am released on the conditions of a probation order`
            `the Minister is informed and satisfied that the conviction has been reversed, the charges have been withdrawn or the proceedings were stayed and not recommenced within the required time period` IS `my conviction has been reversed, the charges withdrawn or the proceedings stayed`
            `all rights of appeal have been exhausted` IS `all rights of appeal have been exhausted`


§§ `The supplement and the top-up that go with the Allowance (ss 22, 22.1)`

-- s 22(2). A pensioner whose spouse or common-law partner is paid an Allowance under section 19 gets the supplement under section 22(2) in place of the
-- Part II supplement.
@export Will I be paid a supplement under section 22(2) instead of under Part II because my spouse or partner has applied for an Allowance (s 22(2))?
GIVEN `an application for my spouse's or partner's Allowance has been made and approved for the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application for an Allowance for your spouse or common-law partner been made and approved for the month?
      `the requirement for that application has been waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the requirement for that application been waived for the month?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will I be paid a supplement under section 22(2) instead of under Part II` IF
    `s 22(2): the supplement under this subsection is payable in lieu of the supplement under Part II` `an application for my spouse's or partner's Allowance has been made and approved for the month` `the requirement for that application has been waived`


-- s 22(7). Where the application for the Allowance is approved, the pensioner's application for the Part II supplement is deemed made and approved.
@export Am I treated as having applied for the supplement under Part II when my spouse or partner's Allowance application is approved (s 22(7))?
GIVEN `an application for the Allowance has been made and approved for my spouse or partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application for an Allowance been made and approved under Part III in respect of your spouse or common-law partner?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as having applied for the supplement under Part II` IF
    `s 22(7): the application is deemed to have been made and approved under Part II` `an application for the Allowance has been made and approved for my spouse or partner`


-- s 22(5). If the Allowance payable to your spouse or partner is suspended or terminated, you may be paid the Part II supplement for the month.
@export May I be paid the Part II supplement again for a month in which my spouse's or partner's Allowance is suspended or has ended (s 22(5))?
GIVEN `my spouse's or partner's Allowance is suspended for the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Allowance payable to your spouse or common-law partner suspended for the month?
      `my spouse's or partner's Allowance is terminated for the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Allowance payable to your spouse or common-law partner terminated for the month?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be paid the Part II supplement again while my spouse's or partner's Allowance is suspended or has ended` IF
    `s 22(5): the pensioner may be paid the amount of supplement provided under Part II for the month` `my spouse's or partner's Allowance is suspended for the month` `my spouse's or partner's Allowance is terminated for the month`


-- s 22(6). The amount of supplement a pensioner may be paid for a month in which the pensioner's spouse or partner is paid an Allowance; blank (NOTHING)
-- where the subsection does not say.
@export How much supplement may I be paid for the month when my spouse or partner is paid an Allowance (s 22(6))?
GIVEN `the Allowance payable to my spouse or partner for the month` IS A NUMBER @desc How much Allowance is payable to your spouse or common-law partner for the month, in dollars?
      `the supplement payable to me under Part III for the month` IS A NUMBER @desc How much supplement is payable to you under Part III for the month, in dollars?
      `the supplement that would be payable to me under Part II for the month` IS A NUMBER @desc How much supplement would be payable to you under Part II for the month, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much supplement may I be paid for the month when my spouse or partner is paid an Allowance` IS
    `s 22(6): the amount of supplement the pensioner may be paid for the month` `the Allowance payable to my spouse or partner for the month` `the supplement payable to me under Part III for the month` `the supplement that would be payable to me under Part II for the month`


-- s 22.1(2). An additional amount added to the Allowance of the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner.
@export How much may be added to my Allowance as the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner (s 22.1(2))?
GIVEN `the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? (give any date in that month)
      `the amount determined for A` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the figure for A in section 22.1 for your quarter, in dollars?
      `my years of residence in Canada after age 18` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years have you lived in Canada since you turned 18, counted to the last day of the previous month?
      `a pension or allowance was payable to me for March 1996 or an earlier month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a pension or an allowance payable to you for the month of March 1996 or an earlier month?
      `a pension or allowance was payable to me for January 2001 or an earlier month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a pension or an allowance payable to you for the month of January 2001 or an earlier month?
      `before March 7, 1996 I was living in Canada as a citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before March 7, 1996, were you living in Canada as a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident?
      `our combined income for the base calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your combined income with the pensioner for the base calendar year, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much may be added to my Allowance as the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` IS
    `s 22.1: the amount that may be added, given the amount determined by the formula` (`s 22.1(2): the amount determined by the formula for a spouse or common-law partner referred to in subsection 22(3)` `the month I am asking about` `the amount determined for A` `my special qualification facts` `our combined income for the base calendar year`)
    WHERE
        `my special qualification facts` MEANS `Special qualification facts` WITH
            `years of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age, as of the last day of the immediately preceding month` IS `my years of residence in Canada after age 18`
            `a pension or allowance was payable to the person for the month of March 1996 or an earlier month` IS `a pension or allowance was payable to me for March 1996 or an earlier month`
            `a pension or allowance was payable to the person for the month of January 2001 or an earlier month` IS `a pension or allowance was payable to me for January 2001 or an earlier month`
            `before March 7, 1996 the person was residing in Canada as a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident` IS `before March 7, 1996 I was living in Canada as a citizen or permanent resident`


-- s 22.1(3). An additional amount added to a survivor's Allowance.
@export How much may be added to my Allowance as a survivor (s 22.1(3))?
GIVEN `the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? (give any date in that month)
      `the amount determined for A` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the figure for A in section 22.1 for your quarter, in dollars?
      `my years of residence in Canada after age 18` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years have you lived in Canada since you turned 18, counted to the last day of the previous month?
      `a pension or allowance was payable to me for March 1996 or an earlier month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a pension or an allowance payable to you for the month of March 1996 or an earlier month?
      `a pension or allowance was payable to me for January 2001 or an earlier month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a pension or an allowance payable to you for the month of January 2001 or an earlier month?
      `before March 7, 1996 I was living in Canada as a citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before March 7, 1996, were you living in Canada as a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident?
      `my income for the base calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was your income for the base calendar year, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much may be added to my Allowance as a survivor` IS
    `s 22.1: the amount that may be added, given the amount determined by the formula` (`s 22.1(3): the amount determined by the formula for a survivor referred to in subsection 22(4)` `the month I am asking about` `the amount determined for A` `my special qualification facts` `my income for the base calendar year`)
    WHERE
        `my special qualification facts` MEANS `Special qualification facts` WITH
            `years of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age, as of the last day of the immediately preceding month` IS `my years of residence in Canada after age 18`
            `a pension or allowance was payable to the person for the month of March 1996 or an earlier month` IS `a pension or allowance was payable to me for March 1996 or an earlier month`
            `a pension or allowance was payable to the person for the month of January 2001 or an earlier month` IS `a pension or allowance was payable to me for January 2001 or an earlier month`
            `before March 7, 1996 the person was residing in Canada as a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident` IS `before March 7, 1996 I was living in Canada as a citizen or permanent resident`


§§ `When an Allowance starts, and how it is paid (ss 23 to 26)`

-- s 23(1). Payment starts in the first month after your application is approved.
@export In which month does payment of my Allowance start (s 23(1))?
GIVEN `the day my application for the Allowance was approved` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your application for the Allowance approved?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `In which month does payment of my Allowance start` IS
    `s 23(1): the first month for which payment of the allowance commences` `the day my application for the Allowance was approved`


-- s 23(1). Where the approval comes after the last day of the month you applied, it may be made effective from a prescribed earlier date, not before the day
-- your application was received; the answer is blank (NOTHING) where it may not.
@export Can my approval be made effective from an earlier date if it was approved after the month I applied (s 23(1))?
GIVEN `the day my application was received` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your application received?
      `the day my application for the Allowance was approved` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your application for the Allowance approved?
      `the earlier date the regulations prescribe` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc What earlier date do the Old Age Security Regulations prescribe for your case? (leave blank if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Can my approval be made effective from an earlier date` IS
    `s 23(1): the earlier date as of which the approval may be effective` `the day my application was received` `the day my application for the Allowance was approved` `the earlier date the regulations prescribe`


-- s 23(1.1). Where the requirement for an application was waived, payment may not start more than eleven months before the month it was waived.
@export How far back may payment of my Allowance start if the Minister waived my application (s 23(1.1))?
GIVEN `the month the Minister waived my application` IS A DATE @desc In which month did the Minister waive the need for you to apply? (give any date in that month)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `How far back may payment of my Allowance start if the Minister waived my application` IS
    `s 23(1.1): the earliest month in which payment of the allowance may commence` `the month the Minister waived my application`


-- s 23(2). If you turned 60 before your application was received, the approval may be made effective from a day not before the later of one year before
-- the day it was received and your 60th birthday; blank (NOTHING) if you had not yet turned 60.
@export How far back may my approval be made effective if I applied after turning 60 (s 23(2))?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day my application was received` IS A DATE @desc On what day was your application received?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `How far back may my approval be made effective if I applied after turning 60` IS
    `s 23(2): the earliest day to which the approval may be made effective` `my date of birth` `the day my application was received`


-- s 23(3). If your application is approved while you are incarcerated, payment starts in the month you are released, but only if you notify the Minister in
-- writing and remain eligible.
@export Does my Allowance start in the month I am released from prison (s 23(3))?
GIVEN `I am described in paragraph 19(6)(f) or 21(9)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person described in paragraph 19(6)(f) or 21(9)(d) of the Act (incarcerated under a qualifying sentence)?
      `my application was approved while I am incarcerated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your application approved while you are incarcerated?
      `I have notified the Minister in writing of my release` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you notified the Minister in writing, before or after your release?
      `I continue to be eligible for an Allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you continue to be eligible for an Allowance?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my Allowance start in the month I am released from prison` IF
    `s 23(3): payment of the allowance commences in respect of the month of release` `I am described in paragraph 19(6)(f) or 21(9)(d)` `my application was approved while I am incarcerated` `I have notified the Minister in writing of my release` `I continue to be eligible for an Allowance`


-- s 24(1). Your right to have the application considered; the Minister's correlative duty is to consider it without delay.
@export Must the Minister consider my application for an Allowance without delay (s 24(1))?
GIVEN `the Minister has received my application for an Allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister received your application for an Allowance?
      `the Minister has waived my need to apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister waived the need for you to apply?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister consider my application for an Allowance without delay` IF
    `s 24(1): the Minister must consider without delay whether the applicant is entitled to be paid an allowance` `the Minister has received my application for an Allowance` `the Minister has waived my need to apply`


-- s 24(2). Your right to be told the basis of the amount.
@export Will the Minister tell me in writing how the amount of my Allowance was worked out, if I ask (s 24(2))?
GIVEN `I have asked for particulars of how my Allowance was fixed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you asked for particulars of the basis on which the amount of your Allowance was fixed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the Minister tell me in writing how the amount of my Allowance was worked out` IF
    `s 24(2): the Minister must forthwith notify the applicant in writing of the basis on which the amount was fixed` `I have asked for particulars of how my Allowance was fixed`


-- s 24(2). Your right to be told of the decision and the reasons.
@export Will the Minister tell me in writing why no Allowance may be paid to me (s 24(2))?
GIVEN `the Minister has decided that no Allowance may be paid to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister decided that no Allowance may be paid to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the Minister tell me in writing why no Allowance may be paid to me` IF
    `s 24(2): the Minister must forthwith notify the applicant in writing of the decision that no allowance may be paid and the Minister's reasons` `the Minister has decided that no Allowance may be paid to me`


-- s 25. Payment is made in arrears at the end of the month, except that payment approved after the end of the first month payable, for the month of approval and
-- the months before it, may be made at the end of the month of approval or of the month after.
@export What is the earliest day on which my Allowance for this month can be paid (s 25)?
GIVEN `the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? (give any date in that month)
      `the first month for which a payment of my Allowance may be made` IS A DATE @desc What is the first month for which a payment of your Allowance may be made? (give any date in that month)
      `the day payment of my Allowance was approved` IS A DATE @desc On what day was payment of your Allowance approved?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the earliest day on which my Allowance for this month can be paid` IS
    (`s 25: the end-of-month days on which payment of the allowance for the month may be made` `the month I am asking about` `the first month for which a payment of my Allowance may be made` `the day payment of my Allowance was approved`)'s `the earliest day`


-- s 25, as above.
@export What is the latest day on which my Allowance for this month can be paid (s 25)?
GIVEN `the month I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which month are you asking about? (give any date in that month)
      `the first month for which a payment of my Allowance may be made` IS A DATE @desc What is the first month for which a payment of your Allowance may be made? (give any date in that month)
      `the day payment of my Allowance was approved` IS A DATE @desc On what day was payment of your Allowance approved?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the latest day on which my Allowance for this month can be paid` IS
    (`s 25: the end-of-month days on which payment of the allowance for the month may be made` `the month I am asking about` `the first month for which a payment of my Allowance may be made` `the day payment of my Allowance was approved`)'s `the latest day`


-- s 26(1.1). The Minister's power to waive; its correlative is your liability to have the requirement waived (no duty to file again).
@export May the Minister waive my having to file information again for the Allowance if I already gave it for the supplement (s 26(1.1))?
GIVEN `I already gave the information for a Part II supplement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already submitted to or filed with the Minister, for an application for a supplement under Part II, the information that subsections 14(1) and 15(1) and (2) require?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Minister waive my having to file information again for the Allowance` IF
    `s 26(1.1): the Minister may waive the requirements of subsections 14(1) and 15(1) and (2) in respect of an application for an allowance` `I already gave the information for a Part II supplement`

